// `?:` is an explicit Result handling operation, not a fallback for any value:
// its scrutinee must already be a Result, and it never reinterprets a plain
// value as `Success`. Accepting this made the fallback unreachable dead code —
// arithmetic yields a plain value; a variable's fallible unary negation
// requires an Arith policy. [PATTERN-RESULT-DEFAULT] [ARITH-EFFECT]
let dead = 5 ?: -1
print("${dead}")
